* ''A page never stands as a vessel'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-29: //"Approve your leans"//, after the mirror-thread talk-story). Every page holds a SURFACE with a port onto a vessel, in every setup: a browser on a node's own box, an anon-device browser vessel, a fleet of equivalent vessels. The no-VM-on-the-main-thread law reads "no sovereign VM and no key on a surface" (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/lararium-canonical-model`>> #/the-laws), and the DreamDOM mirror, a camera carrying a whole engine and no truth, honors it (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom`>> #/open-rulings). Custody follows: the anon-device browser vessel keeps its opened key in its own worker, never in page memory (the per-tab ask stands, and the shared holder still carries no unlock); it seals its store through sealed-store steps 2 and 3; and it takes an unlock ceremony the surface cannot paint, the boundary sitting where the person types the secret (its shape stays research). The full mirror runs people's plugins only after those seal steps land for the browser store; no clear record stands under the full mirror, and the device key rests non-extractable. Browser persona roots already rest sealed once a slot binds (`browser-custody.ts`); only the place seed and veil archives may stand clear before a slot, and the opened tree key in page memory names the exposure this ruling moves.

